not APIs and MCP servers.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.620
So, a SAS-defined agent hits
a roadblock when they try

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.930
to interact with
these applications.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.380
That is why you need
computer-using agents.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.110
Second, the legacy gap.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.320
Enterprises rely on
important applications

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.750
that will not be modernized
in the near term.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.450
These applications
sit on Windows 32,

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.990
which is why you need
computer-using agents

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:10.350
that can have a
Windows computer.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.510
